# Rule: SwiftUI Environment System

Sources

https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/environment-values

Core Principle

The SwiftUI environment is a downward-propagating context system.

Rules

- Use the environment for contextual data that many descendants need to read.
- Prefer explicit parameters for narrow, local dependencies.
- Prefer bindings for editable child-owned interactions.
- Inject environment values high enough to define context, but no higher.
- Override environment values at meaningful subtree boundaries.
- Avoid turning the environment into an unstructured global bag.

Must Not

- Do not hide normal view inputs in the environment.
- Do not put every dependency into the environment because it is convenient.
- Do not replace a clear initializer parameter with environment unless inheritance is genuinely beneficial.
